{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2196-05-01 06:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning, I'm Dr. Lee. I understand you came in with chest pressure last night?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2196-05-01 06:18:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, it woke me up. Felt just like my heart attack before. I took nitroglycerin, but it didn’t help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2196-05-01 06:19:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. You also said it got worse when you took a deep breath?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2196-05-01 06:20:05",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Exactly. I couldn’t catch a full breath, but I wasn’t short of breath. Just pressure."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2196-05-01 06:21:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve reviewed your EKG and your troponin levels—both are normal. That’s good news. It doesn’t look like a heart attack."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2196-05-01 06:22:40",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, thank goodness. But what is it then?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2196-05-01 06:23:55",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re considering inflammation around the heart—called pericarditis. It can cause sharp chest pain that worsens with breathing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2196-05-01 06:25:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Pericarditis? Is that related to my recent pneumonia?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2196-05-01 06:26:25",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, exactly. Viral infections like the parainfluenza you had can sometimes lead to post-viral pericarditis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2196-05-01 06:27:40",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s not my heart muscle, but the lining around it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2196-05-01 06:28:55",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s right. And we’ve ruled out other causes—your chest X-ray was clear, and a V/Q scan showed no pulmonary embolism."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2196-05-01 06:30:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the ultrasound on my legs?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2196-05-01 06:31:25",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No blood clots. That’s reassuring, especially with your history of DVT and PE."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2196-05-01 06:32:40",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I was worried about that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2196-05-01 06:33:55",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We also did an echocardiogram. Your heart function is stable—about 43% ejection fraction, mostly unchanged from before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2196-05-01 06:35:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And no fluid around the heart?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2196-05-01 06:36:25",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No pericardial effusion. That’s another good sign."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2196-05-01 06:37:40",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So what’s the plan?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2196-05-01 06:38:55",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re going to start you on a steroid—prednisone—to reduce the inflammation. It usually works well for pericarditis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2196-05-01 06:40:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been on steroids before. Will it affect my kidney?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2196-05-01 06:41:25",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll monitor closely. Your transplant team is aware. We’re starting low and tapering slowly to minimize risks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2196-05-01 06:42:40",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2196-05-02 07:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. How’s the chest pain today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2196-05-02 07:16:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Better. Still there, but not as intense. I think the prednisone is helping."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2196-05-02 07:17:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great to hear. Your labs this morning show your kidney function is stable, though creatinine is a bit higher—2.5 from 2.0."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2196-05-02 07:18:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that from the steroid?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2196-05-02 07:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. We’ll keep an eye on it. Your potassium was low yesterday, so we gave you some, and it’s improved."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2196-05-02 07:21:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember that. Felt a bit weak."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2196-05-02 07:22:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, low potassium can do that. We’ll keep monitoring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2196-05-02 07:23:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "My mouth feels dry. And I noticed some little sores on the roof of my mouth."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2196-05-02 07:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I’ll take a look. Sometimes steroids or viral infections can cause oral changes. We’ll make sure it’s not an infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2196-05-03 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your pain is continuing to improve, and your breathing is easier?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2196-05-03 08:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, much better. I’m even walking in the hall a little."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2196-05-03 08:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Excellent. We’re going to keep you on the prednisone taper. You’re on day three of 20 mg, then we’ll step down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2196-05-03 08:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my other meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2196-05-03 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Most are continuing. We’ve held amlodipine because your blood pressure has been well-controlled—around 130s over 80."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2196-05-03 08:06:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And the zolpidem?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2196-05-03 08:07:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve switched you to trazodone for sleep. It’s safer with your other medications."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2196-05-03 08:08:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been on that before. It worked well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2196-05-04 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing really well. Pain is minimal, labs are stable. We’re planning for discharge tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2196-05-04 09:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. What about follow-up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2196-05-04 09:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll need a new cardiologist—your previous one has left the practice. You’re scheduled to see a nurse practitioner next week."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2196-05-04 09:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll make sure to call and confirm."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2196-05-04 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Also, please get a Chem 7 blood test done in a few days and send the results to your primary doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2196-05-04 09:06:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll do that. Any restrictions at home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2196-05-04 09:07:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take it easy for a few days. No heavy lifting. Continue the prednisone exactly as prescribed—don’t stop suddenly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2196-05-04 09:08:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I won’t. I know how that goes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2196-05-05 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "All set for discharge. Your pain is resolved, and you’re back to your baseline."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2196-05-05 10:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I was really scared it was another heart attack."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2196-05-05 10:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. But everything points to pericarditis, and you’ve responded well. Keep taking the steroids, and call if the chest pain returns."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2196-05-05 10:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. And I’ll follow up with the NP and get the blood work done."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2196-05-05 10:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. You’re doing great. Take care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2196-05-05 10:06:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Dr. Lee."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2196-05-05 10:07:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You're welcome. Someone will be in shortly with your discharge papers."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2196-05-05 10:08:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. I’m ready to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2196-05-05 10:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll make sure your sister knows you’re on your way."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2196-05-05 10:11:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "She’s been worried. I’ll call her right after."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2196-05-05 10:12:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s a good idea. Stay in touch with your care team, and take it easy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2196-05-05 10:13:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks again for everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2196-05-05 10:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You're very welcome. Get some rest and we’ll see you in follow-up."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2196-05-01 06:17:00",
    "admission_end": "2196-05-05 15:03:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with a history of kidney transplant, coronary artery disease, prior pulmonary embolism, and heart failure presented with sudden-onset substernal chest pressure identical to her prior NSTEMI, which worsened with deep inspiration but was not associated with shortness of breath, fever, or cough. Initial evaluation revealed normal troponins, no ischemic EKG changes, and a normal chest X-ray. A V/Q scan ruled out pulmonary embolism, and an echocardiogram showed stable left ventricular function without pericardial effusion. The chest pain was attributed to post-viral pericarditis following a recent parainfluenza infection. She was started on a prednisone taper, with significant improvement in symptoms. Her amlodipine was held due to well-controlled blood pressure, and zolpidem was replaced with trazodone for insomnia. She was discharged home in stable condition with plans for outpatient follow-up and lab monitoring.",
    "problems": [
      "Infective pericarditis",
      "Hypertensive heart and chronic kidney disease with heart failure and stage 1 through stage 4 chronic kidney disease, or unspecified chronic kidney disease",
